{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor","id":767588,"title":"Celerity sneak attacks, and Bulletproof armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T22:28:10-08:00","id":767588,"title":"Celerity sneak attacks, and Bulletproof armor","content":"Sorry if this topic has come up before, but does anyone know how the celerity sneak attacks work? The last option for spending Vitae is moving really fast.<br /> <br /> &quot;She may use this to briefly avoid detection or launch surprise attacks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean a surprise attack automatically takes place denying an opponent's defense?<br /> -That seems a bit extreme to not let them have a resistance against it.<br /> <br /> Is it just a way to reflexively hide without necessarily needing cover which invokes normal surprise rules (contested roll)?<br /> -That seems dodgy because the Surprise rules say it can only happen in the first round of combat (though I suppose you could ignore that) but more importantly deny a the surprised victim their action for the turn. Which would be a good way to ensure nobody could ever oppose you. Although I suppose that is also a problem with the option above as well.<br /> <br /> My best guess would be to go for the contested roll, but ignore the first round rule and the losing action rule because those are implied effects of an ambush rather than just a sneaky attack, personally, but if anybody has any better ideas, I'd love to hear them.<br /> <br /> I also have a minor question about vampires and bulletproof armor. Since vampires already downgrade all normal weapons to bashing, is wearing bulletproof armor worthless to them (aside from the actual armor bonus)?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that it just wouldn't do anything special unless it was some sort of magical mega-kill bullet that would do lethal to them to start out, and then it would downgrade like a normal bullet from the armor. And, although I don't think there are any rules to support it, I could also see something being downgraded to bashing multiple times not doing anything. Protection for something that's already not going to do anything but bruise you seems trivial and irrelevant (again though, I don't think there's rules to back that up even a little bit).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T03:41:59-08:00","id":767719,"title":"","content":"No, they still provoke the typical surprise check. It doesn't give you automatic hiding either. If, for instance they were out of range for striking someone, celerity would let them suddenly move into range (surprise check) and attack.<br /> <br /> Bullet resistant armor isn't worthless, it's just not as useful to vampires as most others. Three people shooting you and doing 6-9+ bashing damage per turn and you can only heal 2 pts per turn is still going to roll over to lethal fairly quickly so anything that lessens or negates that damage is useful. It's also a good Masquerade preservation tool.<br /> Also there's a lot of people on this forum who gleefully claim to allow headshots and chest shots to retain their lethal damage rating, so in those cases the armor is every bit as useful to vampires as it is normal humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:19:41-08:00","id":767756,"title":"","content":"Okay, so if they still provoke the typical surprise check, then can it only be used in the first round of combat? It would definitely make them lose their action then.<br /> Are you sure it wouldn't allow them to hide (which would be the thing provoking the surprise check)? I only ask because it says that your movement are so sudden that you appear to be shifting from point to point instead of going through the space between. And then it explicitly says you can use it to briefly avoid detection, which wouldn't really mean much if you already needed to be sitting behind cover preparing a normal ambush.<br /> <br /> Well, yes, the armor would still work as armor, and be good for that reason. I was more meaning the bulletproof part of it. Once it rolls over into lethal downgrading doesn't really do anything because it'd all just roll to lethal again.<br /> <br /> That is a good point about the Masquerade preservation though, I guess a person in SWAT gear shrugging off bullets would be a bit less suspicious than someone wearing a hard leather biker jacket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:32:01-08:00","id":767837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=767756#post767756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so if they still provoke the typical surprise check, then can it only be used in the first round of combat? It would definitely make them lose their action then.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you sure it wouldn't allow them to hide (which would be the thing provoking the surprise check)? I only ask because it says that your movement are so sudden that you appear to be shifting from point to point instead of going through the space between. And then it explicitly says you can use it to briefly avoid detection, which wouldn't really mean much if you already needed to be sitting behind cover preparing a normal ambush. </div> </div> </div> Celerity only lets you move really fast. Which, when we're talking about avoiding detection, is a huge boon. Someone glancing away for a second is enough time for you to do something, whereas a normal mortal couldn't. So, if you're role playing out being stealthy, Celerity will definitely help you there with getting from hiding spot to hiding spot when normal speed wouldn't. But that's the only way that Celerity helps with stealth attacks and hiding - getting you into position faster. <br /> <br /> \u200bDoes Celerity let you move fast enough that you're unable to be seen with the naked eye? Maybe, but slow motion cameras and the like will still capture you, and that's only at high levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, yes, the armor would still work as armor, and be good for that reason. I was more meaning the bulletproof part of it. Once it rolls over into lethal downgrading doesn't really do anything because it'd all just roll to lethal again. </div> </div> </div> It depends on individual STs, since there are some who let head (and sometimes heart) shots do lethal, or shot gun blasts, or something. But, assuming that none of those apply, then yes, vampires are already bullet resistant, so kevlar doesn't help with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:40:15-08:00","id":767841,"title":"","content":"I had a hunter set up in a building where the lower floors had lasers on their windows set to, among other things, a security door to the stairs and elevator that would block them off if the lasers were broken. The thief vampire character used celerity to dart from the window to inside the door. So the lasers broke and the security barriers went down but she had already gotten to the other side of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:49:22-08:00","id":767892,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd say seeing a guy 20 feet away from you one moment and then getting sucker punched by him the next would count as a surprise attack, wether or not he's hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:44:09-08:00","id":768066,"title":"","content":"Against mortals or fledgelings, sure. In a vamp on vamp fight, where you are expecting someoen to be able to move that fast, I wouldn't say that was a surprise, since you should expect it at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:09:49-08:00","id":768155,"title":"","content":"Expecting it isn't the same as being able to cope with it. I'd say a vampire could use Celerity to cancel the surprise attack if equal or greater than the attacker's Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:21:10-08:00","id":768158,"title":"","content":"That's what the Clash of Wills rules are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T19:44:39-08:00","id":768241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=768066#post768066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against mortals or fledgelings, sure. In a vamp on vamp fight, where you are expecting someoen to be able to move that fast, I wouldn't say that was a surprise, since you should expect it at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they're expecting a fight. Most of the time when you see a Daeva or a Mekhet 20 feet away, your first instinct isn't &quot;I bet he's going to zip over here and attack me at any moment&quot;, unless there's already some reason to believe they have it out for you. If they're a from a Clan that's not known for their speed, it's probably not even on your mind unless you've seen them use it before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=768155#post768155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expecting it isn't the same as being able to cope with it. I'd say a vampire could use Celerity to cancel the surprise attack if equal or greater than the attacker's Celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to move fast doesn't necessarily mean you can process something else moving fast though. I'd probably allow a character with Auspex to do a Clash of Wills, or a character with Quicken Sight active to just automatically not be surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T19:46:17-08:00","id":768243,"title":"","content":"If you're able to move as fast you should be able to process stuff moving fast. What I was aiming for was Clash of Wills but I forgot it existed.<br /> <br /> I'd allow it for someone who has Celerity or that Auspex/Celerity devotion that lets you perceive high speed things, myself. Just seeing a vampire go into Celerity speeds to attack isn't enough to overcome the advantage, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T06:36:20-08:00","id":768463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=768241#post768241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if they're expecting a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider sucker punches, even by people without magic powers, to be surprise attacks. Your situation holds true, regardless if we're talking about someone with Celerity, or someone without a drop of supernatural power to them. <br /> <br /> And honestly, being attacked, or Discipline used upon, should be an expectation whenever you're meeting another vampire outside of Elysium or close-as-cotorie-mates. We're talking about rival predators who's insticts are to fight over territory and prey. So, yes. If you see a Daeva or Mekhet 20 feet away that you don't fully trust, you should instantly go on your guard. They're a danger. That was the original idea behind the Predator's Taint, and it carries over slightly different, but mostly intact, with the Aura - you feel a predator approaching. The same with Ventrue and Nosferatu - Nightmare and Dominate can reach that far. Gangrel are the only ones that would naturally be less a threat at that distance, and that's assuming we're talking about someone who's not learning any out of clan powers, including sorceries. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Expecting it isn't the same as being able to cope with it. I'd say a vampire could use Celerity to cancel the surprise attack if equal or greater than the attacker's Celerity.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being able to move fast doesn't necessarily mean you can process something else moving fast though. I'd probably allow a character with Auspex to do a Clash of Wills, or a character with Quicken Sight active to just automatically not be surprised. </div> </div> </div>That is already taken into account by the rules, with the whole pre-emptively moving before someone else through using Celerity. There's no need for further rulings on the matter when we already have rules to take care of it. No need to reinvent the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T06:59:22-08:00","id":768476,"title":"","content":"I'd treat it as a firearms attack. If you can dodge a bullet, you can dodge a speedblitzing vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T16:35:32-08:00","id":768782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=768463#post768463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is already taken into account by the rules, with the whole pre-emptively moving before someone else through using Celerity. There's no need for further rulings on the matter when we already have rules to take care of it. No need to reinvent the wheel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Celerity to interrupt Celerity looks like one of the reasons the Clash of Wills rule exists. It would (and should) be invoked for this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T03:48:48-08:00","id":769083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=768782#post768782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Celerity to interrupt Celerity looks like one of the reasons the Clash of Wills rule exists. It would (and should) be invoked for this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. Its even explicitly spelled out in the Celerity rules to use Clash of Wills at this point, so totally spot on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:59:57-08:00","id":769303,"title":"","content":"In my reading, that's for trying to interrupt an opponent's interrupt, not for trying to avoid being surprised by an unexpectedly fast attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:15:10-08:00","id":769315,"title":"","content":"It is, but they're suggesting a vampire avoiding another vampire's unexpectedly fast attack because the attacked vampire has celerity in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:32:36-08:00","id":769333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767588-celerity-sneak-attacks-and-bulletproof-armor?p=769315#post769315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, but they're suggesting a vampire avoiding another vampire's unexpectedly fast attack because the attacked vampire has celerity in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you expect it to happen. Otherwise it would be a surprise attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}